       "say": "**How much does the starting belief matter?** Three people start with different priors and see the same data. After 7 of 10 the flat prior gives 0.667, an **optimistic** prior Beta(20, 2) (as if 22 earlier users had 20 successes) gives **0.84**, a **sceptical** Beta(2, 20) gives **0.28**: with little data the prior dominates. After 70 of 100 they give 0.70, 0.74 and 0.59; after 700 of 1,000 they have **converged** to 0.700, 0.705 and 0.687. Data eventually outweigh any prior that does not rule the truth out. The practical advice: choose a prior you can defend (from earlier experiments, or weakly informative), show that conclusions hold across reasonable priors, and be modest when the data are few."
