       "say": "**Split conformal prediction.** Fit a model on 1,000 training points. On 500 separate **calibration** points compute the absolute error of each prediction (the \"score\"). Take a high quantile of these scores: with a small correction, the `ceil((n + 1) × 0.9)`-th smallest of 500, which is **5.11**. The prediction interval for any new case is the model's prediction **plus and minus 5.11**. On 5,000 fresh test points it contains the truth **89.7%** of the time, as promised (0.9). The model is a plain straight line; nothing about it was checked, and the guarantee still holds. The only ingredients were data the model had not seen and a quantile.",
