       "say": "**The guarantee is about the average, over splits.** Repeat the whole procedure 300 times with different random samples (300 for training, 200 for calibration, 2,000 for testing): the average coverage is **0.900**, as promised. But a single run varies: the standard deviation is 0.023 and 90% of the runs fall between **0.861 and 0.934**. So with 200 calibration points, a single interval might cover 86% or 93%: the guarantee holds on average and fluctuates around it. A larger calibration set reduces the fluctuation, as the next step shows.",
